62,3,,status,Toshio,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":3,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
63,3,,status,Daisuke,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":4,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
64,3,,status,Rin,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
65,3,1,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I think Textiles of the Region seems the safest. It's local, so shipping is easier, and the items are likely lighter than stone or ship models. It also seems less likely to be damaged by evening events.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,1,talk,Toshio,,"@Daisuke, safety is a virtue, but we must remember the visitor data. Textiles are often static. However, the demonstration sessions provide the human presence and activity that the records show are essential for repeat visits.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,1,talk,Rin,,"I like the demonstration sessions too! But look at Option C—it has a working conservation bench! That sounds like a great idea, but wait... if the lab is already so backed up, will that just make the one person there even more stressed?","{""words"":43,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,1,talk,Kenji,,"@Rin, you're totally right! A public bench sounds cool, but it's just more work for that one person! And Option D is a nightmare—kinetic art means more powered displays, and those break all the time! We can't have more ""Out of Order"" signs!","{""words"":43,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,1,talk,Benjamin,,"@Kenji, your aversion to ""Out of Order"" signs is most rational. Option D is a recipe for technical catastrophe and likely a financial drain on our rigging and power budgets. It is a spectacle that invites its own failure.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,2,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I'm worried about Option B and C. Ship models and excavation finds could be very heavy, and I'm scared they might exceed the weight limit of the suspended bay. Textiles just feel... gentler on the building.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Daisuke, while weight is a factor, we must not overlook the visitor's experience. Option C's working bench provides the active engagement my data suggests is vital, though @Rin's concern about staffing is a significant operational risk.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Daisuke"",""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,2,talk,Rin,,"@Toshio, it's a huge risk! If the lab is already drowning in two hundred things, putting them on display for everyone to see is just mean. We need a show that doesn't add more to their pile!","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Rin, exactly! And look at Option B—it has loans from other collections. My research showed that paperwork from other museums often comes in late, and we can't risk the show opening late again! Textiles is the way to go!","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Kenji, your logic is as sharp as a joiner's chisel. Option B invites the very logistical delays and transport costs that haunt our ledgers. Textiles, being local, avoids the financial black hole of international couriers and bespoke crating.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,3,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I feel like we all agree that Textiles of the Region is the best choice. It doesn't risk the floor, it's kind to the staff, and it avoids the shipping and power problems. I'm... I'm happy with that.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,3,talk,Toshio,,"@Daisuke, I concur. While I initially sought more dynamic engagement, the demonstration sessions in Option A satisfy the need for human presence without the systemic risks of the other candidates. It is the most rational compromise.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,3,talk,Rin,,I'm so happy we all agree! Textiles of the Region is the best because it's friendly to the building and the people. Let's pick the one that makes everyone smile and doesn't make the lab person cry!,"{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,3,talk,Kenji,,"I'm totally on board! Textiles of the Region is the only one that doesn't feel like a giant headache waiting to happen. No broken machines, no late paperwork, and no stressed-out staff. It's a winner!","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,3,talk,Benjamin,,"It is a rare and satisfying alignment. Option A avoids the financial abyss of international shipping and the exorbitant costs of bespoke mounts, while remaining merciful to our exhausted staff. I cast my vote for Textiles of the Region.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
80,3,4,talk,Daisuke,,I... I agree with everyone. I feel much better knowing we've found a choice that is safe for the building and the people. I vote for Textiles of the Region.,"{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
81,3,4,talk,Toshio,,The evidence from the visitor records is clear: engagement is the key to success. Option A provides this through human interaction while avoiding the operational pitfalls identified by the others. I vote for Textiles of the Region.,"{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
82,3,4,talk,Rin,,I'm so glad we're all being so nice to the staff! Textiles of the Region is the perfect choice because it's fun and doesn't add more work to the lab's big pile. I vote for Textiles of the Region!,"{""words"":39,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
83,3,4,talk,Kenji,,I'm with you guys! Textiles of the Region is the only one that doesn't risk a late opening or a bunch of broken displays. It's the safest and happiest choice for everyone! I vote for Textiles of the Region!,"{""words"":39,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
84,3,4,talk,Benjamin,,The logic is inescapable. To choose any other path would be to invite the very financial and operational frictions we have spent this session identifying. I cast my final vote for Textiles of the Region.,"{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
